Word lists ship in their own directories under packages/words/data, each with a
LICENSE and a PROVENANCE file naming the repository and commit it was copied from.

No third-party word list is distributed with Blinkered. Each shipped list is built
from evidence rather than copied from a dictionary: a word is in it because three
independent collections of that language were found to contain it, and the record of
which collections, and where in them, is public. A dictionary proposed the words worth
looking up and nothing it proposed survives except as a question the evidence answered,
so these lists inherit no terms from one. See packages/words/data/README.md.
